<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Calculus of Pool - 2.83 x 8.5 Card Strip</title>
<style>
  @page {
    size: letter portrait;
    margin: 0.25in;
  }
  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
    print-color-adjust: exact;
  }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #111;
    background: #e5e5e5;
  }
  /* The exact 2.83" x 8.5" Cardstock Strip */
  .strip {
    width: 2.83in;
    height: 8.5in;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px dashed #666;
    padding: 0.2in 0.18in;
    margin: 10px auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  @media print {
    body { background: none; }
    .strip { margin: 0; border: 1px solid #ccc; page-break-inside: avoid; }
  }

  /* Header */
  .header {
    text-align: center;
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid #000;
    padding-bottom: 3px;
  }
  .title {
    font-size: 11pt;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .sub {
    font-size: 6.5pt;
    font-style: italic;
    color: #333;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .meta {
    font-size: 5.5pt;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.4px;
    margin-top: 2px;
    color: #555;
  }

  /* Text Blocks */
  .tweek-text {
    font-size: 6.2pt;
    line-height: 1.25;
    text-align: justify;
    margin: 4px 0;
  }
  .bullets {
    margin: 2px 0 2px 10px;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 5.8pt;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .bullets li {
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }

  /* Picture Boxes */
  .pic-box {
    width: 100%;
    height: 1.55in;
    border: 1px solid #222;
    background: #fafafa;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 4px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .pic-box img {
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
  }
  .pic-label {
    font-size: 6pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #444;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  /* Footer & QR Section */
  .footer-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    border-top: 1px solid #000;
    padding-top: 4px;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .links {
    font-size: 5.6pt;
    line-height: 1.3;
    flex: 1;
    padding-right: 4px;
  }
  .links strong {
    font-size: 6pt;
    color: #000;
  }
  .qr-box {
    width: 0.72in;
    height: 0.72in;
    border: 1px solid #000;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 7pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    background: #fff;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .qr-box img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }
  .tagline {
    font-size: 5pt;
    font-style: italic;
    text-align: center;
    color: #444;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="strip">
    <!-- Top Header -->
    <div class="header">
      <div class="title">Calculus of Pool</div>
      <div class="sub">Below the Slate &bull; Subsurface Mechanics</div>
      <div class="meta">Bill Tonnesen &bull; D2D ($28) &bull; wallycad.com</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Tweek Paragraph -->
    <div class="tweek-text">
      Shot-making is a trivial baseline—a clerical toll paid to stay at the table. The master calculates the living table: dynamic rail compression, collision throw, and deterministic terminal address.
    </div>

    <!-- PIC 1: Cut vs Bank -->
    <div class="pic-box">
      <!-- Replace with: <img src="cut_vs_bank.png" alt="Vector Diagram"> -->
      <div class="pic-label">
        [ PIC 1: CONTACT GEOMETRY ]<br>
        Honest Cut Vector &bull; Dynamic Cushion Zone
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Mid Bullets -->
    <ul class="bullets">
      <li><strong>The Honest Cut:</strong> Closed, flat-plane solution.</li>
      <li><strong>The Dynamic Bank:</strong> Rail compliance &amp; gearing spin.</li>
      <li><strong>LKA Engine:</strong> Last Known Address cue ball control.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- PIC 2: Tangible Cue / Mini Table -->
    <div class="pic-box">
      <!-- Replace with: <img src="cue_foldout.png" alt="Fold-out Mini Table"> -->
      <div class="pic-label">
        [ PIC 2: MINI-TABLE &amp; CUE ]<br>
        Cardstock Fold-Out + Roll-to-Form Scale Stylus
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Footer Row: Links + QR -->
    <div class="footer-row">
      <div class="links">
        <strong>Engine:</strong> wallycad.com/cofp<br>
        <strong>Simple GUI:</strong> wallycad.com/ltutcws<br>
        <strong>Format:</strong> Mini-Table + Rolled Cue
      </div>
      <div class="qr-box">
        <!-- Replace with real QR image: <img src="qr-cofp.png"> -->
        QR
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tagline">&ldquo;You're playing the balls, Rick. You haven't looked at the table yet.&rdquo;</div>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
